ights\n- Transition assistance, data continuity, and wind-down terms\n- Assignment, change-of-control, liability caps, and indemnities\n\n**Naming dependencies**\n- Fund name, ticker, prospectus, and marketing references to the index\n- Rule 35d-1 name-policy implications and shareholder notice requirements for changes\n- Exchange listing rules and SEC filing lead times\n\n**Affiliated-information issues**\n- Whether the index provider or calculation agent is affiliated with the adviser, sponsor, or an authorized participant\n- Access to rebalance or constituent information, and information barriers\n- Revenue sharing or related-party fees, and whether Section 15(c) review applies\n- Prospectus disclosure of any affiliation\n\n**Contingency**\nIdentify candidate replacement indexes in advance, but do not assume substitution rights exist. Confirm them against the actual contract and with counsel.","ttft_ms":6950,"type":"result","duration_ms":8399,"uuid":"5007fc60-14df-44df-af7e-c03ed07fbc10","ttft_stream_ms":425,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":425,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
